#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:529
msgid "Core"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:77
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Demo Importer so you can import "
"one of the Total live demos. Demos are to be used as a \"starter\" for a new "
"site and are best imported on a fresh WordPress installation."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:83 inc/under-construction.php:37
#: inc/under-construction.php:38
msgid "Under Construction"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:86
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Under Construction where you can "
"select a custom page and have your entire website redirect to this page for "
"any visitor that is not logged in. Logged in users will be able to browse the "
"site normally."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:91
msgid "Bundled/Recommended Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:94
msgid ""
"Enables a notice that displays a list of bundled or recommended plugins for "
"the theme. It also adds an admin screen under Appearance > Install Plugins "
"for installing and updating bundled plugins. This feature also provides "
"updates to the bundled plugins whenever there is a theme update which "
"includes an updated version of a bundled plugin."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:100
#: inc/customizer/settings/general/dark-mode.php:64 inc/dark-mode.php:97
msgid "Dark Mode"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:103
msgid ""
"Enables a \"Dark Mode\" tab under Customize > Global Styles to assign dark "
"colors to your main site colors, the ability to assign a dark color variation "
"to your color palette colors as well as the ability to enable a light/dark "
"toggle button for your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:109 inc/theme-builder/theme-builder.php:172
msgid "Dynamic Templates"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:112
msgid "Enables the Dynamic Templates dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:117
msgid "Theme Elements"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:120
msgid ""
"Enables over 60 custom builder blocks exclusive to the Total theme for "
"WPBakery. These modules are located inside the Total Theme Core plugin. By "
"default the modules will load regardless of the WPBakery plugin allowing you "
"to use the blocks as standard shortcodes if you are using a different builder "
"such as Elementor."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:126
msgid "Custom CSS"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:128 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:136
msgid "Developers"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:129
msgid ""
"Enables the Custom CSS admin panel for making CSS customizations via the "
"backend. This function hooks into the core WordPress custom CSS functionality "
"so any CSS added here will also be available in the Customizer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:134 inc/custom-actions.php:36
#: inc/custom-actions.php:37
msgid "Custom Actions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:137
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Custom Actions where you can "
"insert HTML/JS to any of the theme’s core action hooks. It’s a great way to "
"add global content anywhere on your site. PHP input is not supported for "
"security reasons. For more advanced modifications it is adviced to use a "
"child theme."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:147 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:156
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:167 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:176
msgid "Post Types"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:165
msgid ""
"When enabled, a new \"Connect to Staff Member\" option will be added to the "
"user profile settings page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:182 inc/blog/single-blocks.php:20
#: inc/cpt/single-blocks.php:36 inc/integration/custom-post-type-ui.php:157
#: inc/integration/post-types-unlimited.php:191
msgid "Post Series"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:185
msgid ""
"Enables a new taxonomy named Post Series to your standard posts which allows "
"you to \"connect\" different posts together as a series. For any post in a "
"series, the front end will display links to all other posts in the series. "
"This is commonly used for multipart tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:191 inc/theme-builder/header-builder.php:53
#: inc/theme-builder/header-builder.php:54
msgid "Header Builder"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:194
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Header Builder where you can "
"select any template to override the default theme header. This functionality "
"is compatible with both WPBakery and Elementor if you want to create a page "
"builder based header."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:199 inc/theme-builder/footer-builder.php:57
#: inc/theme-builder/footer-builder.php:58
msgid "Footer Builder"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:202
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Footer Builder where you can "
"select any template to override the default theme footer. This functionality "
"is compatible with both WPBakery and Elementor if you want to create a page "
"builder based header."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:207
msgid "Custom WP Login Screen"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:210
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Custom Login where you tweak the "
"default WordPress login screen such as uploading a custom logo and changin "
"the default background and form colors."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:215
msgid "Custom 404 Page"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:218
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Custom 404 where you can redirect "
"your 404 pages or select a custom template for your 404 page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:223 inc/customizer/manager.php:26
#: inc/customizer/manager.php:27
msgid "Customizer Manager"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:225 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:388
msgid "Optimizations"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:226
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Customizer Manager where you can "
"select what theme tabs are displayed in the Customizer. For example if you do "
"not plan on using the theme Top Bar or Toggle Bar functionaility you can hide "
"the settings completely in the Customizer to slim things down and speed "
"things up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:234
msgid "Remove Elementor Upsells"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:236 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:245
msgid "Elementor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:237
msgid ""
"When enabled, the theme will attempt to remove as many Elementor upsell "
"prompts as possible, helping to declutter the admin area and eliminate "
"unnecessary distractions."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:243
msgid "Elementor Container Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:246
msgid ""
"Enables compatibility between the theme's layout and Elementor. It removes "
"the default left and right padding applied to containers in Elementor and "
"sets the width and max width for the outermost containers to match the "
"settings defined under Customize > Layout. This helps align your Elementor-"
"created pages with the overall design of the site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:251
msgid "Custom WordPress Gallery"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:254
msgid ""
"Enables a custom output for the \"legacy\" WordPress gallery (non-gutenberg) "
"that includes lightbox functionality and custom image cropping via the "
"settings under Theme Panel > Image Sizes > Other. If you are using Elementor "
"it is recommended that you disable this setting to prevent conflicts because "
"the plugin also creates a custom output for galleries."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:261
msgid "Custom Widget Areas"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:263 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:279
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:288
msgid "Widgets"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:264
msgid ""
"Enables a dashboard at Appearance > Widget Areas for creating and assigning "
"custom widget areas."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:269
msgid "Card Builder"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:271 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:354
msgid "Post Cards"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:272
msgid ""
"Enables the Custom Cards panel which allows you to build your own custom post "
"card designs."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:277
msgid "Theme Widgets"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:280
msgid "Enables over 20 custom widgets exclusive to the Total theme."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:286
msgid "Widget Block Editor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:289
msgid "Enables the widget block editor in WordPress 5.8+."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:295
msgid "Taxonomy Thumbnails"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:297 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:305
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:313 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:321
msgid "Taxonomies (categories)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:298
msgid ""
"Enables the ability to define a thumbnail for your categories and custom "
"taxonomies. This thumbnail is used on the front-end as the page header "
"background and is also used in various elements such as the Categories Grid "
"and Categories Carousel modules."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:303
msgid "Taxonomy Thumbnail Page Header"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:306
msgid ""
"When enabled taxonomy terms that have thumbnails defined will display the "
"page header background style using the thumbnail as the background."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:311
msgid "Taxonomy Theme Settings"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:314
msgid ""
"Enables extra options within the Theme Settings metabox when editing "
"categories and other taxonomies (redirection, sidebar, card entry style, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:319
msgid "Taxonomy Colors"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:322
msgid ""
"Enables the ability to set custom colors for your categories which may be "
"used by various theme elements and card styles. This functionality is enabled "
"for categories only but can be extended to custom taxonomies via a filter."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:328
msgid "Image Gallery Metabox"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:330 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:337
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:344
msgid "Custom Fields"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:331
msgid ""
"Enables the \"Image Gallery\" metabox in the post editor which allows you do "
"define gallery images for your pages, posts, portfolio items and custom post "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:335 inc/integration/post-types-unlimited.php:167
msgid "Theme Settings Metabox"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:338
msgid ""
"Enables the \"Theme Settings\" metabox in the post editor that allows you to "
"alter various Customizer settings on a per post basis. For most, this feature "
"isn't necessary and can be disabled to slim things down. Disabling this "
"feature will only remove the non post type specific settings."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:342
msgid "Post Media Custom Fields"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:345
msgid ""
"Enables the Media tab for defining your post video, audio or other media."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:352 inc/integration/post-types-unlimited.php:183
msgid "Card Settings Metabox"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:355
msgid ""
"Enables the Card Settings metabox in the post editor that allows you to alter "
"various card settings on a per post basis. Disabling this feature will only "
"remove the fields from the post editor, any previously set values will still "
"be applied."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:362
msgid "Editor Styles"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:364 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:372
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:380
msgid "Editor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:365
msgid ""
"Loads custom styles when using the WordPress editor so that your fonts and "
"certain styles match the live site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:370
msgid "Editor Formats"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:373
msgid ""
"Enables the \"Formats\" button with some default and custom styles that you "
"can use when adding text via the WordPress editor."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:378
msgid "Editor Shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:381
msgid ""
"Enables a new \"Shortcodes\" button in the WordPress editor with some "
"exclusive theme shortcodes including line break, icon, current year, "
"searchform, button, divider and spacing. You can easily add new shortcodes to "
"this dropdown via a child theme."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:386
msgid "Remove WP Emojis"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:389
msgid ""
"By default WordPress adds scripts to the admin and frontend to render custom "
"WP emoji icons. This is unnecessary bloat and thus disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:394 inc/image-sizes.php:130 inc/image-sizes.php:131
#: inc/integration/custom-post-type-ui.php:185
#: inc/integration/post-types-unlimited.php:214
msgid "Image Sizes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:397
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Image Sizes where you can define "
"custom cropping for the images on your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:402
msgid "Page Animations"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:405
msgid ""
"Enables a new tab under Appearance > Customize > General Theme Options > Page "
"Animations where you can enable a loading icon when people visit your website "
"as well define load in and load out animations for your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:411
msgid "Color Palette"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:414
msgid ""
"Enables the Color Palette admin panel for registering your site's color "
"palette."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:419
msgid "Font Manager"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:421 inc/admin/theme-panel.php:430
#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:548
msgid "Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:422
msgid ""
"Enables the Font Manager admin panel for registering fonts for use on the "
"site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:428
msgid "Typography Options"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:431
msgid ""
"Enables a new tab at Appearance > Customize > Typography where you can define "
"custom fonts and font styles for various parts of the site including the main "
"body, menu, sidebar, footer, callout, topbar, etc."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:436
msgid "Page Edit Links"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:439
msgid ""
"Enables edit links at the bottom of your posts and pages so you can quickly "
"access the backend or front-end editor while logged into your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:444
msgid "Import/Export Panel"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:447
msgid ""
"Enables a new admin screen at Theme Panel > Import/Export where you can "
"quickly export or import Customizer settings from one site to the other. This "
"is useful when switching to a child theme or if you wanted to copy a backup "
"of your settings before making changes in the Customizer (you can copy the "
"settings and paste them into a text file on your computer)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:454
msgid "WPBakery Theme Mode"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:457
msgid ""
"Enables \"Theme Mode\" for the WPBakery page builder plugin. This disables "
"the License Tab under the WPbakery admin settings and hides some unnecessary "
"notices and about pages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:462
msgid "WPBakery Design Options"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:466
msgid ""
"Enables the \"Design Options\" tab in the WPBakery plugin settings which is "
"disabled by default to prevent theme conflicts and keep the site slimmer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:475
msgid "WPBakery Slim Mode"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:479 inc/health-check/wpbakery-slim-mode.php:27
msgid ""
"Exclusive theme feature that removes redundant WPBakery elements and their "
"CSS to greatly slim things down. Enabling this option will also hide elements "
"intended for dynamic templates and custom cards from showing up when editing "
"posts and pages. If enabling on an existing site you will need to double to "
"ensure you are not using any of the elements removed by this function and if "
"so, replace them."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:484
msgid "WPBakery Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:487
msgid ""
"Enables theme Patterns for WPBakery which you can access when inserting "
"templates."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:492
msgid "WPBakery Field Info Tooltips"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:495
msgid ""
"By default various WPBakery page builder editor fields include extra info "
"about the field to help you use it. Previously, these displayed below the "
"fields, but in WPBakery v7.7 they added an info icon next to the field "
"heading instead. If you don't like looking at all the info icons and you "
"understand how to use theme you can disable this feature to clean up the "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:500
msgid "WPBakery Optimized JS"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:503
msgid ""
"By default WPBakery loads their main javascript file and the jQuery library "
"whenever any builder element is present on the page. By enabling this option "
"the theme will check to make sure the scripts are absolutely necessary and if "
"not will remove them from the page prior to rendering to speed up your site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:508
msgid "WPBakery CSS Stretch Sections & Rows"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:511
msgid ""
"The theme will use CSS (where possible) for your Section and Row Stretch "
"settings instead of the default javascript based WPBakery stretching."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:518
msgid "WooCommerce Integration"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:521
msgid ""
"Enables theme modifications for the WooCommerce plugin including custom "
"styling and modifications. Disable for testing purposes or to use WooCommerce "
"in it's native/vanilla form."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:527
msgid "Thumbnail Post Format Icons"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-panel.php:531
